BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cinema Dissection: Cinephile's Spooky Choice
DTSTART:20251011T170000Z
DTEND:20251011T231500Z
DTSTAMP:20251011T170000Z
UID:GQ7JSWwp2L
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 360 mins (6h00m)\n\nFilm Talks The votes are in! The
  winning film is The Witch. Join us for the scene-by-scene breakdown of Ro
 bert Egger's American Gothic debut feature film. This year SIFF celebrates
  the Halloween spooky season by allowing our audience members to determine
  which horror genre classic will be the subject for our October cinema dis
 section. Will it be Robert Eggers’s American Gothic debut feature film\,
  The Witch? Perhaps you prefer David Robert Mitchell’s paranoid supernat
 ural chiller\, It Follows? Maybe John Landis’s consummate blend of terro
 r\, gore\, and comedy\, An American Werewolf in London? Or The Hunger\, To
 ny Scott’s erotic revisionist vampire thriller? Whichever film wins the 
 vote\, join SIFF Programmer Dan Doody and local filmmaker Jeremy Cropf for
  a scene-by-scene deconstruction of a terrifying classic film guaranteed t
 o haunt your nightmares. Vote\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/
 education/adult-film-education/film-talks/cinema-dissection-cinephiles-cho
 ice-spooky\n\nEstimated start: 10:15
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
