BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Water and Power (1989)
DTSTART:20251017T020000Z
DTEND:20251017T031000Z
DTSTAMP:20251017T020000Z
UID:Qv9NtmdyFy
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 55 mins (0h55m)\n\nPresented by Mount Analogue ○ 
 Art + Cinema Winner of the Grand Jury Prize for Documentary at the 1990 Su
 ndance Film Festival\, Water and Power\, presented in its original 35mm fo
 rmat\, is artist and filmmaker Pat O'Neill's masterwork that explores the 
 complex relationship between water and the city of Los Angeles.\n\nhttps:/
 /www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/water-and-power-35mm\n\nEstimated start: 
 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Refract Glassblowing Film Festival: Opening Night
DTSTART:20251018T013000Z
DTEND:20251018T043000Z
DTSTAMP:20251018T013000Z
UID:o7U6c1Qf8R
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 165 mins (2h45m)\n\n6:30pm | SIFF Film Center  Pres
 ented by Glass Art Society and Chihuly Garden and Glass  The Glass Art S
 ociety (GAS) in partnership with Chihuly Garden and Glass invite you to jo
 in us for the opening night of the 2025 GAS Film Festival. Enjoy the inter
 section of glass and film. Enjoy light snacks with words from Executive Di
 rector of GAS\, Brandi Clark and Executive Director of Chihuly Garden and 
 Glass\, Michelle Bufano. Followed by the showing of the winner of the 2025
  GAS Film Festival.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/glass-art-s
 ociety-film-festival-opening-night\n\nEstimated start: 18:45
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
